-- title:
--   Power series with non-unit constant term acquire a root
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative local ring that is complete and separated for the adic topology of its maximal ideal $\mathfrak m =$ `IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A`, and let $F \in A[[X]]$ be a formal power series with $\mathrm{constantCoeff}(F) \in \mathfrak m$ whose coefficientwise reduction along the residue map $A \to A/\mathfrak m$ is nonzero in $(A/\mathfrak m)[[X]]$. Let $\Omega$ be an algebraically closed field which is an $A$-algebra, and let $V \subseteq \Omega$ be a valuation subring such that $\mathrm{algebraMap}\,A\,\Omega$ maps $A$ into $V$ and maps every element of $\mathfrak m$ into the non-units of $V$. Then there is a ring homomorphism $\varphi \colon A[[X]] \to V$ such that: $\varphi(C(a))$ equals the image of $a$ in $\Omega$ for every $a \in A$; $\varphi(X)$ lies in the maximal ideal of $V$; $\varphi(G)$ lies in the maximal ideal of $V$ whenever $\mathrm{constantCoeff}(G) \in \mathfrak m$; for every $G$ the residues in $V/\mathfrak m_V$ of $\varphi(G)$ and of $\varphi(C(\mathrm{constantCoeff}(G)))$ agree; $\varphi(X)$, viewed in $\Omega$, is integral over $A$; every $\varphi(G)$, viewed in $\Omega$, lies in the $A$-subalgebra generated by $\varphi(X)$; and $\varphi(F) = 0$.
--
--   This is the existence of a zero of $F$ in the maximal ideal of a valuation ring dominating $A$, in the form obtained from the Weierstrass preparation and division theorems over a complete local ring: $F$ becomes a distinguished polynomial up to a unit, and $\varphi$ is evaluation at one of its roots, which is integral over $A$ and of positive valuation. It is used in the construction of valuation-ring lifts compatible with Vélu quotients and their action on two- and three-torsion.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_PowerSeries_exists_ringHom_valuationSubring_map_eq_zero_of_constantCoeff_mem_maximalIdeal.lean

